      "body": "### 项目名称 / Project\n**SQL Mysteries**\n\nhttps://github.com/Namanlashkari/sql-mysteries\n\nPlay online: https://namanlashkari.github.io/sql-mysteries/\n\n### 一句话介绍 / One-liner\nThree 10-minute SQL mysteries (hackathon sabotage, coffee-recipe leak, esports aimbot). Write a `SELECT`, run it against live SQLite, get scored.\n\n### 为什么适合 HelloGitHub / Why it fits\n- Beginner-friendly: 3 tables per case, story clues instead of “use HAVING”\n- Zero install in the browser (sql.js) or `python3 launch.py` locally (stdlib only)\n- Result-set validation: any correct query passes, not string matching\n- Progressive hints that cost points; solutions stay off the page source in the local server\n\n### 截图 / Screenshots\nRepo README has three case screenshots: `screenshots/hackathon.png`, `coffee.png`, `esports.png`.\n\n### 作者 / Author\nNaman Lashkari — https://github.com/Namanlashkari\n\nI built this as a hiring-drive / teaching tool. Happy to add a Chinese blurb if useful.",
